{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"baca2b76098793ba","name":"card_event_strike_from_the_forest","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_strike_from_the_forest","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"STRIKE FROM THE WOODS","text":"Pin target unit. Add a SISSI to your support line.","flavorText":"The Battle of Tolvajärvi, fought on 12 December 1939 in Ladoga Karelia, was the first large offensive victory for Finland during the Winter War. The Finnish side had 4,000 men (16th Infantry Regiment, 4 separate battalions and one artillery battalion) against 20,000 Soviet soldiers of the 139th Rifle Division (9 infantry battalions, 60 artillery pieces, one scout battalion, one signal battalion, one sapper battalion, 30 tanks, and 376 aircraft), and despite being outnumbered 5 to 1, the Finns won a convincing victory. The Finnish side lost over 100 soldiers, with 250 others injured, while the Soviet Union suffered significant losses, with an estimated 5,000 soldiers killed and the capture of many of their weapons and equipment, including artillery pieces, tanks, and machine guns. This battle was a big win for the Finnish forces and lifted the morale of the entire Finnish Army. After this successful counter-attack, there were no major battles in this area, and only infrequent gunfire occurred. The Finnish troops held their position there until the end of the Winter War.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_strike_from_the_forest","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_strike_from_the_forest_title","SourceString":"STRIKE FROM THE WOODS","LocalizedString":"STRIKE FROM THE WOODS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_strike_from_the_forest_text","SourceString":"Pin target unit. Add a SISSI to your support line.","Loca